## Goal
Perform principal component analysis (PCA) on gene-level counts to visualize how treated and untreated samples separate in the expression space. This analysis will identify the primary axes of variation across the six samples and show whether the treatment effect (treated vs. untreated groups) is the dominant source of variation.

