## Method
1. Load the gene counts matrix (genes × samples) and the design table (sample_id, condition, group, replicate) using Python (conda environment: gars-bio).
2. Filter genes: keep only genes with mean count ≥ 1 across all samples to remove low-abundance genes with negligible signal.
3. Normalize counts using log2(count + 1) transformation to stabilize variance across the count range.
4. Center and scale each gene (subtract mean, divide by standard deviation) to weight all genes equally in PCA.
5. Perform PCA using scikit-learn's PCA on the scaled counts, extracting all principal components.
6. Compute variance explained by each of the first 10 principal components.
7. Create a scatter plot (figure) showing PC1 vs. PC2 with points colored by treatment condition (untreated = blue, treated = red) and sized by replicate to visualize sample grouping.
8. Export PCA coordinates for all samples and all principal components to a CSV table.

